public import Mathlib.Data.Int.Basic

/-!
# Explicit tables for the root cuts LL20 and LL22 (data)

The cross signs `ς_{jk}` and the matrix `𝐇` at `p ≡ 3 (mod 4)` of the root cuts LL20 and LL22
(`paper/sections/25_upper_reference.tex`, `subsec:record:upper_root`, `cert:record:direct-star`)
as explicit `36 × 36` tables, rows and columns in the order of the plus-half index
(`Sarkozy.SpectralD.Root.slotCode` for LL20, `slotCode / 2` for LL22: the slots `(u₀, u₁, ℓ)` of
`U⁺` in lexicographic order). The tables of `𝐇` store `𝐇_{kl} + 1 ≥ 0` (`tableEntryShift`
subtracts the one), since long integer literals with signs elaborate slowly. This file holds only
the data; the agreement with the Lean objects is proved in `Sarkozy.SpectralD.RootTables`.

New material for this paper.
-/

@[expose] public section

namespace Sarkozy.SpectralD.Root

/-- Entry `(i, j)` of a table given by its rows (`0` outside it). -/
def tableEntry (t : List (List ℤ)) (i j : ℕ) : ℤ := (t.getD i []).getD j 0

/-- Entry `(i, j)` of a table of shifted entries, minus one (`-1` outside it). -/
def tableEntryShift (t : List (List ℕ)) (i j : ℕ) : ℤ := ((t.getD i []).getD j 0 : ℤ) - 1

